=== email subject
[Action needed by 3 Oct 2026] 30 actively exploited flaws in your products
=== email body
Patchtacio found 30 known exploited vulnerabilities (CISA KEV) that affect products on your list. Attackers are already using all of them. Start with the earliest deadline.
Patchtacio matched them by product name and has not checked whether your versions are affected.

New:
1. [Action needed by 3 Oct 2026] Fortinet FortiOS: actively exploited flaw (CVE-2026-10006)
   Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel Vulnerability. Added to CISA's list 28 Sep 2026.
   What to do: check the vendor advisory for the fixed version: https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-060
   If you cannot update yet, follow CISA's required action: "Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, follow applicable BOD 22-01 guidance for cloud services, or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable."
   Details: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-10006
